1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,600
I'm your China Travel Expert.
我是你的中国旅游专家

2
00:00:01,600 --> 00:00:04,000
In Guangzhou, breakfast can last three hours.
在广州，早餐能吃三小时

3
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:06,400
They call it yum cha — "drink tea."
广东人管它叫"饮茶"

4
00:00:06,400 --> 00:00:08,800
The rule: one pot of tea, two small plates.
讲究"一盅两件"

5
00:00:08,800 --> 00:00:11,200
Steamer towers of dumplings, buns and tarts.
一笼笼虾饺、叉烧包、蛋挞

6
00:00:11,200 --> 00:00:13,600
When someone pours your tea, tap two fingers.
有人给你倒茶，用两指轻叩桌

7
00:00:13,600 --> 00:00:16,000
It's a silent thank-you — a finger kowtow.
那是无声的谢礼——叩手礼

8
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:18,400
Double-tap if you'd sit here till noon.
想坐到中午的，点个赞

9
00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:20,800
The ritual dates to Qing-era Guangzhou trade.
这习俗源自清代广州通商

10
00:00:20,800 --> 00:00:24,000
★ Expert Tip: Go before 9am, order har gow with a pot of pu'er — and tap to say thanks.
内行贴士：9点前去，点虾饺配普洱，记得叩手

11
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:27,000
Tea first, or dim sum first — your call?
你会先喝茶，还是先夹点心
